# Pisga — work carefully, do not break what works

Read `docs/PISGA-HANDOVER.md` (what was done, how to run, the open list) and `CLAUDE.md` before changing anything.

- Branch `feat/pisga-paint` lives only in this worktree, with 19 commits that are not pushed. Never delete the worktree or reset the branch.
- Before and after every change, run `verify-pisga-fences.mts`, `verify-pisga-terrain.mts` and a free render (`PT=0`). The checks must not get worse than the baseline in the handover. Compare the kindergarten views (kg-*) image by image.
- Change shared rules (`ringRailing`, `nearGuard`, `groundAt`) only when every site case is understood. Fix a single spot inside a coordinate-bounded region, with a comment saying why.
- No paid AI calls (Gemini / image painting) without the user's explicit approval. No push, merge or PR unless asked: Vercel bills every push.
- No bare `git stash`, no `reset --hard`, no killing leftover node/Chrome processes, no DB migrations (local dev hits production), no edits to `.env.local`.
- Railing tags on stairs must contain "stair", or the fence checker calls them floating.
- Talk to the user in full Hebrew only (עברית מלאה): plans, questions, reports, explanations. Do not mix English into user-facing sentences. Keep file paths, shell commands, view IDs, and commit subjects as-is. Code and commit messages stay in English with Co-Authored-By. End every report with a link to the results folder.
